From 695f4a5779b72c91facaad0c5425698508742fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:33:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Onboarding: drive the flow from a screens config array

The flow was 8 hardcoded {step === N && ...} blocks. Going to 22 screens
that way means renumbering every block each time one is inserted, which is
the exact drift the redesign is removing.

Now: one screens: ScreenDef[] array. Each entry owns its id, jumper label
and render. Screen count is derived from it in all four places that used
to read TOTAL_STEPS - the nextStep clamp, OnboardingShell, the progress
bar, and the DEV jumper (which had its own hardcoded 8-label array and
would have silently gone stale). TOTAL_STEPS is gone; there is nothing
left to forget to update.

WeekAct now contributes five flat entries via weekScreens() instead of
being one nested sub-flow, so the progress bar counts real screens rather
than reporting five as one.

Verified: 12 jumper entries, 12 progress segments, every screen renders at
390px, Back walks in reverse across the week-act boundary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
