From 346f89453663914ab68132f6d74839115312c485 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:38:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Onboarding: split the numbers step into six screens
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The old step 7 was the worst screen in the flow: seven inputs at once —
name, age, experience, height, weight, activity level — three separate
keyboard summons and two unit toggles, sitting immediately before the
payoff. That is the last place a form should appear.

Now six screens, one question each, via numberScreens() in NumbersAct.tsx.
Age, height and weight are Dials instead of number fields; each still lets
you tap the number and type, so nobody who prefers the keyboard is trapped.
Experience and activity level become ChoiceCards with a line of context
each, replacing two <Select> dropdowns.

Two real bugs fixed while splitting:

- Switching cm/ft or kg/lb used to CLEAR the field. Tapping the wrong unit
  first cost you the number you had just entered. It now converts.
- The weight question's reassurance is on the weight screen, underneath
  the input, rather than nowhere. That is where the hesitation is.

Also unified the choice button. There were three copies - Onboarding.tsx's
CardBtn, WeekAct.tsx's Choice, and the inline gender buttons - already
drifted on text colour, height and tick behaviour. One ChoiceCard in
kit.tsx now, with hideCheck for the small square tiles.

Verified at 390x844 with the DEV panel hidden: all six new screens render
with the CTA anchored at the same y (812) and no page scroll; height
round-trips 6'1" -> 185cm -> 6'1" across a unit switch; 17 jumper entries
and 17 progress segments agree.

Known, not a regression: screens 1 (Start) and 10 (Around) still scroll -
they are the remaining un-split blocks and are next in Phase 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Scm7SUW7vqCiNscvTtGQQR
